  "step_3": "The information relevant to the decision reason (skewness) is not present in the verbal report. The individual does not consider the distribution of probabilities in terms of left-skewness. Instead, they rely entirely on expected value. The decision reason requires evaluating whether one lottery has a greater probability mass on favorable outcomes (i.e., more left-skewed), which would imply a concentration of probability on the positive outcome. In this case, B has a higher probability (25%) of a positive outcome than A (20%), so B is less left-skewed (more right-skewed). Thus, A is not more left-skewed than B. The individual's reasoning is based on expected value, not skewness. Therefore, the decision reason was not used. The individual did not evaluate or reference skewness in their justification. Hence, the decision reason was not used.",
